SHIP TYPES MODELS

-[x] Pirate → Brigantine
Fast, aggressive, versatile. Classic pirate silhouette with mixed sails and lots of rigging.

-[x] Merchant → East Indiaman
Large cargo vessel with heavy hull and trade-focused design. Feels wealthy and important.

-[x] Navy → Ship of the Line
Massive multi-deck warship with rows of cannons. Instantly communicates military power.

-[x] Slaver → Galley
Oar-powered, cramped, brutal-looking. Fits the human misery vibe extremely well.

-[x] Cartographer → Caravel
Exploration ship. Compact, elegant, long-range, discovery-focused.

-[] Bounty Hunter → Sloop-of-War
Small military pursuit vessel. Fast enough to chase targets, armed enough to win fights.

-[x] Viking → Longship
Obvious choice, but for good reason. Distinct silhouette and iconic identity.

-[x] Fisherman → Cutter
Small practical working vessel. Functional and believable for coastal survival.